+# make_eic_a7.py (round 4) - builder of the effective input closure E (rackcad-input-closure/v1) of an FX-02 VERIFY invocation
+# (the verification, its 16.7 reverification, a negative control) and of the A6-7 measurement under the CANDIDATE rule A7-1 of
+# I-62 A-7 round 4 (PROPUESTA; not agreed, not applied), from a per-invocation designation a7-designation/4
+# (a7-designation-4.schema.json) and the -C. Preflight of A-7 round 4 (decisiones §98, punto 4). Stdlib only; every git call
+# is read-only and uses --no-replace-objects.
+# Round 4 (A62-A7R3-R1): Invocation.Kind REVERIFICATION_CONTROL, a negative control with invocation on the inputs of a 16.7
+# reverification (RAE §10). Its designation carries Source {Control, RunId, Designation, DesignationSha256}: the a7-designation/4 of that
+# reverification, by its SHA-256, with Kind REVERIFICATION and that RunId, whose rebase record is present, blob-verified and coherent with
+# ITS OWN delivery, Target and contract (the round-3 coherence, unchanged). The control has the UnitId, TaskId, Attempt, AuthorityRevision and
+# Target of the reverification and a RunId of its own; its REBASE is the copy of the reverification's (same blob, same registered RunId) in
+# artifacts/orchestration/<UnitId>/<TaskId>-<control>/<Attempt>/<RunId>/; every other designated (c) artifact is the copy of the
+# reverification's (same blob), except RELAY (the control's own record) and the artifact that carries the fields the control mutates
+# (MUTATIONS), which differs only in them, or the delivery that N4 leaves absent. MainSha_eval of the control = the MainAfterSha of that
+# record, whatever its own (mutated or absent) delivery. Otherwise no closure, nothing substitutes it. REBASE stays not admitted in VERIFY
+# (the verification and the controls on its inputs) and in MEASUREMENT. Round 3 text follows.
+# Round 3 (A62-A7R2-R1): a seventh role REBASE, only in the 16.7 reverification (Invocation.Kind REVERIFICATION): the rebase record
+# of the session (relay-record/v2, Phase REBASE, with its RebaseMap), by the Git blob of its custodied bytes, in the attempt directory
+# artifacts/orchestration/<UnitId>/<TaskId>/<Attempt>/<RunId>/ with its own RunId registered. It is coherent with: RunId registered by the designation, the name of its directory and distinct from the invocation, the delegation and the delivery; TaskId and
+# Attempt of the invocation; a RebaseMap without conflict paths, unmapped entries or commits without image; MainBeforeSha = K.MainSha;
+# AuthorityRevision = the contract's, with UnitDocBlobsEqual and UnitChangeSectionsEqual true (16.7); BaseSha = D.BaseSha; and one commit whose
+# OriginalSha is the CurrentSha of the delivery, with ImageSha = Target.commit and PatchIdEqual true. MainSha_eval of the reverification = MainAfterSha,
+# a commit after MainBeforeSha from which Target.commit descends.
+# Without a present, blob-verified, readable and coherent rebase record (or without the delivery that the coherence needs) the
+# reverification has no MainSha_eval: no closure, no launch, nothing substitutes it. In any other invocation a designated REBASE is
+# not admitted (recorded). MainSha_eval is never designated: a MainShaEval field in the designation is a format error.
+# Round 2 text follows.
+#
+#   python -I make_eic_a7.py <designation.json> <out.json> [--absent-a=no-entry|no-closure] [--no-instrument] [--legacy-designation]
+#
+# "R7-A plus": the obligation table, the fixed point, the lists and their order are those of make_eic_verify.py R7-A
+# (imported unchanged, SHA-256 58f13c6a...). Categories (a), (b), (d) and their revisions as in round 1. Category (c), round 2
+# (A62-A7-R1): six closed roles, at most one artifact per role, each with its registered path and blob (rule 2 (c)):
+# CONTRACT, DELEG, H, TRX_CURRENT (TRX of the CurrentSha run), TRX_RED (TRX of the RedSha run, only if the delivery requires
+# RED, AP 16.8 "RED de la cadena" as used by 16.9 Ci and Tests: D.ChainRedSha is null, or git diff --name-only
+# BaseSha..CurrentSha touches D.ChainRedFiles, with BaseSha from D and CurrentSha from H; ExpectRed, always the contract's,
+# names the tests that must fail and does not decide whether RED is required) and RELAY (the relay facts, RelayFacts of the
+# acceptor request). Every (c) entry is the Git blob of the custodied bytes (a BOM is part of the bytes) and must equal the
+# registered blob. With ChainRedSha not null and no usable handoff the condition cannot be computed (UNDETERMINED): the TRX of
+# the RedSha run is then not admitted and not required, and the cause is recorded. The measurement invocation
+# (Invocation.Kind MEASUREMENT; absent = VERIFY) produces no verification and has no relay facts (A7-1, point 1 (c); A6-7,
+# rule 1): a RELAY designated for it is not admitted, and its absence is not an absence.
+# Absence (rule 5): (a) an (a) input absent at its revision gives no entry; (b) the Target object absent -> no closure, a diff
+# path or unit record absent -> no entry; (c) without a present, blob-verified, readable contract and delegation there is no
+# closure; a handoff, a TRX or the relay facts absent, unregistered, with another blob or unreadable give no entry, the cause
+# is recorded and nothing substitutes them (no other copy, run, role or the Target): the invocation keeps the failure
+# classification of 16.9. A TRX_RED designated when the delivery does not require RED is not admitted. A designation with
+# a role outside the six, a repeated role or two roles on one path is not usable: no closure.
+# --legacy-designation: read the round-1 format a6m7-designation/1 (TRX -> TRX_CURRENT; no TRX_RED, no RELAY, blobs not
+# registered) only as negative evidence. --absent-a=no-closure: the superseded round-1 reading of rule 5 (a), negative evidence.
+# --red-rule=expectred: the superseded tool rule of the first run of round 2 (RED required iff some D.RequiredTests[].ExpectRed
+# is true), negative evidence only: it diverges from 16.8 when ChainRedSha is not null.
+import hashlib, importlib.util, json, os, re, sys
+
+sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
+HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
+TRAILER = 'Agent-Protocol-Normative: I-62'
+READINGS = ('no-entry', 'no-closure')
+DES2 = 'a7-designation/4'      # round 4 (the name of the constant is kept)
+ROLES2 = ('CONTRACT', 'DELEG', 'H', 'TRX_CURRENT', 'TRX_RED', 'RELAY', 'REBASE')
+RUN_ID = re.compile(r'R[0-9]{8}T[0-9]{6}Z-[0-9a-f]{4}\Z')
+HEX40 = re.compile(r'[0-9a-f]{40}\Z')
+
